-- Integers and fractions in one column. Nothing here is extreme, but every prefix rounds, so the sum, the product and the mean all land on values that a reassociated accumulation would miss by an ulp.
-- The == lines are the load-bearing pins: they compare inside the backend rather than through the 1e-9 comparator, and they are exactly the law the mean's finish once broke.
--! registry ../registries/141-mixed-scales.reg

--! out 6.6
+/ Mix

--! out 1 1.1 3.1 3.3 6.3 6.6
+\ Mix

--! out 0 0 0 0 0 1
(+\ Mix) == (+/ Mix)

--! out 0.036
*/ Mix

--! out 1 0.1 0.2 0.04 0.12 0.036
*\ Mix

--! out 0 0 0 0 0 1
(*\ Mix) == (*/ Mix)

--! out 1.1
avg/ Mix

--! out 1 0.55 1.0333333333333334 0.825 1.26 1.1
avg\ Mix

--! out 0 0 0 0 0 1
(avg\ Mix) == (avg/ Mix)

--! out 3
max/ Mix

--! out 0.1
min/ Mix
